==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|furiously}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|furious|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfjʊə̯ɹi.ə̯sli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-furiously.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adverb===
{{head|en|adverb}}

# In a [[furious]] manner; [[angrily]].
#: {{ux|en|He glared '''furiously''' at the offender.}}
# [[quickly|Quickly]]; [[frantically]]; with great [[effort]] or [[speed]].
#: {{ux|en|He tried '''furiously''' to get it to work before the deadline.}}
#* {{RQ:Haggard She|passage=Again we set to and bailed '''furiously'''. Fortunately the storm had now quite gone by[.]}}
# [[intense|Intensely]], as with [[embarrassment]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Clara Mille|title=Under The Southern Cross|page=86|passage=Craig, who at twenty was taller than his father, blushed '''furiously''' as he practically threw two small boxes on the table in front of the twins. “Happy birthday”, he managed.}}

